[{:db/id "q-126921/selection/cc138f4904bffee51b6d1c9479183ce0e6771e6d8134be5cb0349215828ebdbf" :answer/id #uuid "4e291f10-eac8-5118-a744-1c754ab2b3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126921/selection/871c5174e6ae7f2b8b50126c53999470baf0195d9031e74778279cb0f36da414" :answer/id #uuid "a99a637b-f75a-5bd3-8aca-2dbc6513b0df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126921/selection/be8d7482996b6e473b7f0563b0f2b06130bf35586d177daead678667c7a811b7" :answer/id #uuid "e795cc2e-1c35-55b2-a55e-6b487a6505fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ -x\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126921/selection/a888b8d212f70b277a2a5d09d1315c773db71e4cd0b1786ee0c30a280c7dc778" :answer/id #uuid "a11f718c-8495-5429-afd8-5751fd26eb02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126921/selection/7d9de9ce88a3fcd30dec3abc002d3ecd65ae45103ef87786923e478b13508744" :answer/id #uuid "03e228b3-ea11-58a0-b53c-2fc041457b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126921/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f4786a8-145a-572c-aeef-afd1f4d4920f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126921/selection/7d9de9ce88a3fcd30dec3abc002d3ecd65ae45103ef87786923e478b13508744" :answer-field/choices ["q-126921/selection/cc138f4904bffee51b6d1c9479183ce0e6771e6d8134be5cb0349215828ebdbf" "q-126921/selection/871c5174e6ae7f2b8b50126c53999470baf0195d9031e74778279cb0f36da414" "q-126921/selection/be8d7482996b6e473b7f0563b0f2b06130bf35586d177daead678667c7a811b7" "q-126921/selection/a888b8d212f70b277a2a5d09d1315c773db71e4cd0b1786ee0c30a280c7dc778" "q-126921/selection/7d9de9ce88a3fcd30dec3abc002d3ecd65ae45103ef87786923e478b13508744"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126921" :question/id #uuid "d45dd63c-10bf-5009-8d17-f860f39bde5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-126921" :question/problem "The closed curve $C$ is defined as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3.$ Find the outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C.$" :question/worked-solution "We can parameterize $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{′}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}=\\sqrt{3},\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126921/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f59392c4-996f-5b29-9c37-7a1b75ffd896"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126921"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126923/selection/b535f7f49407bfbcbc8e413ce0ed16daf88c0e36857fc168b46f78a469e764e4" :answer/id #uuid "c62a56bf-ea4f-5794-9315-e3807b48ec77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126923/selection/7c16cf9a18a126094fe780c662534f4fba023312b8d976ed0bf275c46048f9a6" :answer/id #uuid "a22fc778-d5e3-5d4f-bd21-cdf2cc4c08b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126923/selection/5e9c875c456e1d2157633887ba14e34ac0d95f199fe5486f6384b7a31c8f6c66" :answer/id #uuid "d9ee63ac-e434-5087-992a-d6a4e80cb4d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126923/selection/24ccc1a67e965931f0b53edc1474ee47d48afc1e20f3c1aa191de2cf0f0db346" :answer/id #uuid "366bae8c-726f-542e-bf94-fe7f1b1eabf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126923/selection/30d8b5f7088639ad23e225c387052c84a6aed17222b971bddf29cbc1ade92045" :answer/id #uuid "cb84497f-cacd-537c-a5fb-8b0f3c3f5